## 5. Measured sizing (do not invent)

From `results/uf_graph_sizes.csv` (phenom/circuit, rounds\(=d\), \(p=0.003\)):

| Noise | d | \(V\) (nodes) | Syndrome bytes \(\lceil V/8\rceil\) | Observables |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| phenom | 3 | 72 | 9 | 1 |
| phenom | 21 | 12262 | 1533 | 1 |
| circuit | 3 | 392 | 49 | 1 |
| circuit | 17 | 31478 | 3935 | 1 |
| circuit | 21 | 50722 | 6341 | 1 |

Ring of depth 4 at circuit d=21 ≈ **25 KiB** syndrome SRAM — URAM/BRAM-comfortable. SoA working set (~9.5 MiB at circuit d=21) is **not** the host ring; it is PE/table state (Helios-n / multiplexing territory).

Validated Stim PE-mesh decode today: circuit **d=3 r=3** \(V=392\) \(E=556\) (M47) — natural first H10 TB target when RTL starts.

